  "description": "JUQSUM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H94 N4 Ni5 O36 Tb3 1+,6(H2 O1),N1 O3 1-. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.152-3.787 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.96-105.85°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni5Tb3(L)4(μ-OH)2(μ3-OH)6(o-val)2(H2O)6]NO3·7H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
